Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:04:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Join metrics HTTP fixture threads before interpreter
 exit

Cause: daemon request handlers survive server_close and stalled replies can log BrokenPipeError during interpreter finalization. Existing tests checked only client worker lifetime and deadline assertions, not server fixture lifetime.

Own and join serve/request threads and suppress only expected disconnect errors at the handler boundary. Preserve real stall/trickle timing and every original assertion.

Proof: parent RED on surviving handler; daemon and omitted-serve-join mutants killed. 1115 focused and cross-cutting tests pass, including real sockets, gated ownership, clean subprocess stderr/exit, and exception controls. Independent review approved.
